st":1893,"last":2025,"intercept":-209.1524955376405,"slope":0.1284252241023928,"total":17.0},"snow_normal":47.8},"titles":{"year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, no daily record lows","records":"St. Cloud has nearly stopped setting record lows","change":"St. Cloud's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days show no clear change.","rain":"St. Cloud has gotten wetter"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 40\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13 was a typical day","p_yest":"The high of <strong>40\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 41\u00b0F, and the record is 71\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>18\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"St. Cloud has nearly stopped setting record lows","p_rec":"If St. Cloud's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, St. Cloud has set <strong class=\"sig\">31 standing record lows</strong>, far fewer than the 74 that chance alone would give, and <strong>94 record highs</strong>, more than the 74 that chance alone would give. The 1930s hold the most record highs of any decade (62). St. Cloud's all-time high is 107\u00b0F, on July 22, 1934.","t_chg":"St. Cloud's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days show no clear change.","p_chg":"Across 125 complete years: St. Cloud's average low shows no clear change: +0.07\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.03 to +0.17) that includes zero. St. Cloud's average high shows no clear change: +0.08\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.02 to +0.18) that includes zero. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.87\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.32 to +1.42) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 1 of 12 months. Highs rose in 2 of 12 months.","t_rain":"St. Cloud has gotten wetter","p_rain":"St. Cloud's yearly precipitation has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.25 inches per decade</strong> (95% range 0.00 to +0.50), about +3.3 inches since 1894. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 28.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 2019 (41.92 in); the driest, 1910 (14.64 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":true,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 4 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}